---
import "../styles/global.css";

const effectiveDate = "July 2, 2026";
const contactEmail = "maintainer@example.com";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Luxel privacy policy for the native macOS recorder and Luxel marketing website."
    />
    <meta name="apple-itunes-app" content="app-id=6780682473" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/luxel-icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="alternate" href="/llms.txt" type="text/markdown" title="Luxel LLM-readable index" />
    <link rel="alternate" href="/llms-full.txt" type="text/markdown" title="Luxel full Markdown documentation" />
    <title>Privacy Policy - Luxel</title>
  </head>
  <body class="privacy-page">
    <header class="privacy-topbar">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Luxel home">
        <img class="brand-mark" src="/luxel-icon.svg" alt="" width="48" height="48" />
        <span>Luxel</span>
      </a>
      <nav aria-label="Privacy page navigation">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <a href="/docs">Docs</a>
        <a href="/support">Support</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main class="privacy-shell">
      <section class="privacy-hero" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</p>
        <h1 id="privacy-title">Your recordings stay yours.</h1>
        <p>
          Luxel is built as a local-first Mac app. We do not track you, run analytics,
          sell data, or send your recordings, screenshots, audio, transcripts, or exports
          to a Luxel service.
        </p>
        <p class="privacy-date">Effective date: {effectiveDate}</p>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-content" aria-label="Privacy policy">
        <article>
          <h2>Summary</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Luxel does not collect personal data from the Mac app.</li>
            <li>Luxel does not use advertising SDKs, tracking pixels, analytics, or data brokers.</li>
            <li>Luxel does not sell, rent, share, or monetize your personal data.</li>
            <li>The support form collects only the email address and message you choose to send.</li>
            <li>Your app content stays on your Mac unless you choose to export, share, or move it.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>What Luxel Processes Locally</h2>
          <p>
            Luxel records and edits the content you choose: screen video, system audio,
            microphone audio, camera preview overlays, replay buffer clips, transcripts,
            exports, settings, presets, history, and related caches. This processing happens
            on your Mac. Luxel does not upload this content to us.
          </p>
          <p>
            Transcription uses local Apple speech recognition and, when enabled, local Apple
            Intelligence turn segmentation provided by macOS. If the required local capability
            is unavailable, Luxel does not fall back to a cloud transcription service.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>Permissions</h2>
          <p>
            macOS may ask you to grant Screen & System Audio Recording, Microphone, Camera,
            Speech Recognition, file, folder, or automation permissions. Luxel uses those
            permissions only to perform the feature you request. We do not use permissions
            to build profiles, track behavior, or collect analytics.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>Data Collection</h2>
          <p>
            The Luxel Mac app does not transmit personal data to Luxel or third-party partners
            in a way that lets us access it. That is why Luxel's intended App Store privacy
            posture is Data Not Collected.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you contact us for support, we will receive the information you choose to send,
            such as your email address, message, and any files or screenshots you attach. We use
            that information only to respond to your request, troubleshoot the issue, and keep
            records needed for support, security, or legal compliance.
          </p>
          <p>
            The website support form stores your email address and message in our private support
            workflow so we can track and respond to the request. Only people helping operate
            Luxel support may see those submissions.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>No Sale or Tracking</h2>
          <p>
            Luxel does not sell personal information. Luxel does not share personal information
            for cross-context behavioral advertising. Luxel does not track you across apps,
            websites, or services owned by other companies.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>Website and App Store</h2>
          <p>
            The Luxel marketing website is a static website. We do not intentionally place
            analytics scripts, advertising cookies, tracking pixels, or fingerprinting code on it.
            Our hosting provider, Vercel, may process standard request metadata such as IP address,
            browser user agent, requested URL, timestamp, and security events to deliver, secure,
            and operate the site.
          </p>
          <p>
            The support form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to reduce automated spam. Cloudflare may
            process technical request data necessary to verify that the submission is legitimate.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you open the Mac App Store listing, Apple processes the App Store page, download,
            purchase, update, refund, and account activity under Apple's own terms and privacy
            policy. Luxel does not receive your recordings, transcripts, exports, or app content
            through Apple.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>Updates</h2>
          <p>
            Mac App Store builds receive updates through Apple. If Luxel is distributed separately
            outside the Mac App Store, update checks may contact an update server only when update
            checks are enabled. Update checks are not analytics and are not used for advertising
            or tracking.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>Retention and Deletion</h2>
          <p>
            Recordings, exports, transcript caches, replay buffer files, and settings remain on
            your Mac until you delete them, clear app data, or remove the app. You can delete
            exported files wherever you saved them. Support messages are retained only as long
            as reasonably necessary for support, security, business records, or legal obligations.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>Children</h2>
          <p>
            Luxel is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
            information from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information
            to us, contact us so we can delete it.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>Changes</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy if Luxel's privacy practices change, if the app's features
            change, or if legal requirements change. The effective date above shows when this
            policy was last updated.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            For privacy questions or requests, email
            <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .privacy-page {
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 84% 12%, rgb(22 184 199 / 0.16), transparent 28rem),
      linear-gradient(180deg, #030405 0%, #080b0f 44%, #020304 100%);
  }

  .privacy-topbar {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 10;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 6rem;
    padding-inline: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 4.25rem);
    border-block-end: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.12);
    background: rgb(3 5 7 / 0.72);
    backdrop-filter: blur(24px);
  }

  .privacy-topbar nav {
    display: flex;
    gap: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .privacy-topbar a:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .privacy-shell {
    width: min(calc(100% - 2.5rem), 68rem);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
  }

  .privacy-hero {
    max-width: 52rem;
    padding-block-end: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .privacy-hero h1 {
    max-width: 11ch;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    line-height: 0.92;
  }

  .privacy-hero > p:not(.eyebrow) {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-block-start: 1.35rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 2vw, 1.45rem);
  }

  .privacy-hero .privacy-date {
    color: var(--quiet);
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .privacy-content {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-block-end: 4rem;
  }

  .privacy-content article {
    padding: clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    border: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.12);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.045);
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgb(255 255 255 / 0.08);
  }

  .privacy-content h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.7rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .privacy-content p,
  .privacy-content ul {
    margin-block: 0.85rem 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .privacy-content ul {
    padding-inline-start: 1.2rem;
  }

  .privacy-content li + li,
  .privacy-content p + p {
    margin-block-start: 0.7rem;
  }

  .privacy-content a {
    color: var(--cyan);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .privacy-topbar {
      min-height: 4.75rem;
      padding-inline: 1rem;
    }

    .privacy-topbar nav {
      gap: 1rem;
      font-size: 0.92rem;
    }

    .privacy-shell {
      width: min(calc(100% - 1.25rem), 68rem);
      padding-block: 2.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
